# .lycheeignore — URLs lychee should NOT check
#
# lychee reads exactly one such file, so this repo-root copy replaces the shared one from
# megalint-config: the shared entries are copied below, repo-specific ones are at the end.
#
# Format: one regular expression per line, matched against the extracted URL.
# Lines starting with `#` are comments.
#
# Curation principle: only ignore URLs that cannot resolve by design. A link
# that is merely slow or rate-limited belongs in lychee's retry and accept
# settings; a link that is genuinely broken must be fixed, not ignored.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# URLs assembled at runtime
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# lychee extracts the literal source text, so template placeholders are never
# substituted. A shell `${VAR}` survives verbatim (or percent-encoded as
# `$%7BVAR%7D` when it follows the host), and a GitHub Actions `${{ ... }}`
# expression truncates at the `$` because `{` cannot appear in a URL. All three
# forms produce a request to an address that only exists once the job expands
# it, so the result says nothing about link health.
^https?://.*(\$\{|\$%7B|\$$)

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# in-toto predicate type URIs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `cosign attest --type=<uri>` takes a namespace identifier, not a fetchable
# document — cosign uses the URI verbatim as the statement's predicateType.
# cosign.sigstore.dev has no DNS record at all, so the check fails as a
# connection error on every run regardless of network conditions.
^https://cosign\.sigstore\.dev/attestation/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repo-specific exclusions
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# docker-compose.yml health-check and OTLP endpoints address compose services
# (or the container's own loopback), which only resolve inside the compose network.
^https?://(localhost|jaeger|nats)(:[0-9]+)?(/|$)
